  "body": "@wanderview and I spent a morning trying to figure out whether [code unit less than](https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#code-unit-less-than) matches code point comparison (or, equivalently, UTF-8 byte comparison). It does not.\r\n\r\nThe reason is surrogates. But at first I thought it was only unpaired surrogates, so that if you had two USVStrings you would be safe. @dbaron pointed out that was incorrect and you can get different results for code unit vs. code point sorting even with USVStrings.\r\n\r\nWe should update Infra with at least the following examples, plus probably a few less exciting ones. https://icu-project.org/docs/papers/utf16_code_point_order.html has some good info and examples as well.\r\n\r\n- U+FF61 is \"code unit greater than\" U+10002 since 0xFF61 > 0xD800 0xDC02, even though it is \"code point less than\".\r\n- Similarly U+FB00 (ﬀ) is \"code unit greater than\" U+10478 (𐑸) since 0xFB00 > 0xD801 0xDC78, even though it is \"code point less than\".",
